// T13 — A boundary change is proposed, ratified, rejected or withdrawn
// Source of record: docs/sidd/round30/pass7-domain-spec.md ("S:n" = its line n) and the accepted ADRs docs/adrs/SIFT-ADR-0*.md.
// Founder ruling 2026-11-04: Source = "Spec of record". NDD-SOURCE section 6 gives thread structure and titles only; where it differs from the spec, the spec wins.
//
// STORY FLOW (founder ruling bd996f3e, 2026-11-07, "15 story flows, branches inside"): the main path runs from the start of the thread to its T13.O13 terminal, in the order the spec tells it.
// Every alternative of the thread, once a flow of its own, is a branch at the moment where it diverges: a [branch] moment that holds its deciding event as a plain node (moved from the main path, not copied), an empty first arm `TheMainPath` (the walk takes the first arm when none is chosen, so the main path is the one that goes on after the moment) and one `when` arm for each alternative,
// each ending at its own exit ([outcome] when it is a normal outcome of the thread, [terminal] for a failure or a refusal) or falling through into the moments that follow. Moment derives one scenario for each path. A refusal is a precondition of a command; Moment 0.9.0 derives its negative scenario for every path of the flow (ADR-042). A branch moment that nothing precedes (the first node of the flow, or one whose deciding event is the only node of the previous branch moment's main arm) keeps its first arm `TheMainPath` with the main path's next nodes: no event to anchor on (docs/sidd/round30/story-flows-log.md, 0.9.0 rework).
// A branch arm cites the former flow it carries in its first comment line (the old-to-new mapping is in docs/sidd/round30/story-flows-log.md).
// BRANCHES:
//   T13.M1 · A boundary change is stated or found: GapSourcedMergeRatified (former flow t13-a-gap-sourced-duplicate-merge-is-ratified.moment)
//   T13.M1 · A boundary change is stated or found: GapSourcedMergeRejected (former flow t13-a-gap-sourced-proposal-is-rejected.moment)
//   T13.M1 · A boundary change is stated or found: GapSourcedMergeWithdrawn (former flow t13-a-gap-sourced-proposal-is-withdrawn.moment)
//   T13.M1 · A boundary change is stated or found: NewRootAnswer (former flow t13-a-new-root-answer-proposes-the-root-once.moment)
//   T13.M1 · A boundary change is stated or found: ProvisionalRetired (former flow t13-a-provisional-boundary-construct-is-retired.moment)
//   T13.M1 · A boundary change is stated or found: Retire (former flow t13-a-retire-is-ratified.moment)
//   T13.M1 · A boundary change is stated or found (continued): DuplicateMerge (former flow t13-a-duplicate-merge-is-ratified.moment)
//   T13.M1 · A boundary change is stated or found (continued): DuplicateMergeWhenTheProposalIsNotOpen (former flow t13-a-duplicate-merge-is-ratified.moment)
//   T13.M1 · A boundary change is stated or found (continued): Rename (former flow t13-a-rename-is-ratified.moment)
//   T13.M1 · A boundary change is stated or found (continued): RenameWhenTheProposalIsNotOpen (former flow t13-a-rename-is-ratified.moment)
//   T13.M2 · The proposal is made: StaleVersions (former flow t13-a-stale-proposal-is-withdrawn-in-the-same-write.moment)
//   T13.M2 · The proposal is made: StaleVersionsRatifiedBy (former flow t13-a-stale-proposal-with-ratifiedby-is-withdrawn.moment)
//   T13.M3 · An operator is asked: RatifiedInline (former flow t13-a-boundary-change-is-ratified-inline.moment)
//   T13.M4 · An operator ratifies: Rejected (former flow t13-a-boundary-change-is-rejected.moment)
//   T13.M4 · An operator ratifies: RejectedWhenTheProposalIsNotOpen (former flow t13-a-boundary-change-is-rejected.moment)
//   T13.M4 · An operator ratifies: Withdrawn (former flow t13-a-boundary-change-is-withdrawn.moment)
//   T13.M4·B2 · when the proposal is not open: Move (former flow t13-a-move-is-ratified.moment)
//   T13.M4·B2 · when the proposal is not open: Replace (former flow t13-a-replacement-is-ratified.moment)
//   T13.M4·B2 · when the proposal is not open: ARatifyCascadeWithdrawsAProposalMadeStale (former flow t13-a-ratification-cascade-withdraws-a-stale-proposal.moment)
//   T13.M4·B2 · when the proposal is not open: ARejectCascadeWithdrawsAProposalMadeStale (former flow t13-a-rejection-cascade-withdraws-a-stale-proposal.moment)
// DIFFERENCE FROM NDD-SOURCE (spec wins): The NDD chain walked ratify, reject and withdraw in sequence on one proposal (T13.M4, M5, M6) and listed
//   the per-change ratification steps together; they are exclusive (S:883-889), so each is its own branch.
// DIFFERENCE FROM NDD-SOURCE (spec wins): T13.M2·B1 (a duplicateMerge's pair is not two distinct live constructs) lives in the duplicate-merge branch
//   as Propose's precondition RefusedPairNotDistinctLive (S:861): a derived negative scenario, no branch moment. T13.M1·B1 (a NewRoot answer) is its own
//   flow.
// DIFFERENCE FROM NDD-SOURCE (spec wins): M3 no longer repeats BoundaryChangeProposed to fake a triggered-by: the trigger is the previous node.
// carried from the former main flow, its description: description "T13 — A boundary change is proposed, ratified, rejected or withdrawn (O13). The ratified path for an ImpliesBoundary{new}. Spec of record S:826-898."
// Part of the model directory; validate with `moment parse model/` (project mode) and `moment test` on this file.

flow "T13 — A boundary change is proposed, ratified, rejected or withdrawn"
  description "T13 — A boundary change is proposed, ratified, rejected or withdrawn. The story of the thread from its start to its T13.O13 outcome, with its alternatives as branches at the moment where each diverges. Source of record: docs/sidd/round30/pass7-domain-spec.md."

  lane design "DesignModel" [Core]
  lane clarification "Clarification" [Core]

  moment "T13.M1 · A boundary change is stated or found" [branch]
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story
      design: PlacementDecided  // S:436,487 ImpliesBoundary{new}: a New BC, Aggregate or Relationship construct (DecidePlacement is T3.M3's)
    when GapSourcedMergeRatified
      // former flow: t13-a-gap-sourced-duplicate-merge-is-ratified.moment
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, its header: Separate flow of T13 (a Gap source, S:886 "A Gap-sourced merge also gets the Gap disposal"). The entry-sourced merge is t13-a-duplicate-merge-is-ratified; the Ratify and Reject refusal arms (NoneUnauthorised, RatificationRefused{NotOpen}) are drawn there and the same commands carry the same preconditions here.
      // T13.M1 · A boundary Gap is found
      design: GapOpened  // S:811 "ContextMap Propose(duplicateMerge, source: this Gap"
      // A Boundary Gap proposes a duplicateMerge at most once per open period; the Propose ID derives from the Gap event (S:863).
      // T13.M2 · The proposal is made
      design: Propose  // S:811 "ContextMap Propose(duplicateMerge, source: this Gap, observed boundary versions from that event's finding)"
        triggered-by GapOpened  // S:811 "Boundary → ContextMap Propose(duplicateMerge" (policy BoundaryHandlingProposesDuplicateMerge)
      design: BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:851 "else → BoundaryChangeProposed"
      // T13.M3 · The architects are asked
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:882 "Recipient for a Gap source: all architects, cascading to admins and owners."
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:880 "BoundaryChangeProposed (not ratifiedInline, not withdrawn in the same write)" (policy BoundaryChangeProposedAsksQuestion)
      clarification: QuestionAsked  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule"
      // T13.M4 · An operator ratifies
      clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Answer  // S:1124 "BoundaryChangeProposed → Ratify or Reject"
      clarification: QuestionResolved  // S:1034 "QuestionResolved {generation, resolution: an answer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy"
      design: Ratify  // S:832 "Ratify(proposal, answeredBy, answer ref)"
        triggered-by QuestionResolved  // S:1124 "BoundaryChangeProposed → Ratify or Reject" (policy RoutingProposalAnswerRatifies)
      design: BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:855 "otherwise → BoundaryChangeRatified"
      design: SupersedeConstruct  // S:876 "the newer duplicate (by the older, the survivor)"
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:885 "SupersedeConstruct(by: successor | none, cause: Ratified) for each construct the change retires" (policy BoundaryChangeRatifiedSupersedesRetired)
      design: ConstructSuperseded  // S:555 "ConstructSuperseded {cause, Pointer?, pass?}"
      design: MarkSameAs  // S:886 "for a duplicate merge, also MarkSameAs"
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:886 "for a duplicate merge, also MarkSameAs, carrying the proposal" (policy BoundaryChangeRatifiedMergesDuplicate)
      design: MarkedSameAs  // S:557 "MarkedSameAs {LineageLink, addition?}"
      design: AddAlias  // S:886 "AddAlias on the survivor for each name of the newer duplicate"
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:636 "BoundaryChangeRatified for a duplicateMerge → AddAlias on the survivor" (policy RatifiedDuplicateMergeAddsAliases)
      design: ConstructAliased  // S:616 "ConstructAliased {name, Pointer}"
      design: DisposeGap  // S:821 "BoundaryChangeRatified → DisposeGap(Resolved{SameAs})"
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:820 "Gap-sourced proposals (by ContextMap outcome)" (policy GapSourcedProposalRatifiedDisposesGap)
      // T13.O13 · The Gap is resolved (terminal)
      design: GapResolved [outcome]  // S:752 "GapResolved {resolution, rationale?, computedBy?, carriedFrom?}"
      // PROVES: BoundaryChangeRatified then GapResolved {SameAs} (S:821, S:1333).
    when GapSourcedMergeRejected
      // former flow: t13-a-gap-sourced-proposal-is-rejected.moment
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, its description: description "T13 — a duplicateMerge proposed by a Boundary Gap is rejected by an operator: the Gap is disposed Resolved{Distinct}, which is then Covered and not asked again. Spec of record S:822, S:833, S:858-859, S:1334."
      // T13.M1 · A boundary Gap is found
      design: GapOpened  // S:811 "ContextMap Propose(duplicateMerge, source: this Gap"
      // A Boundary Gap proposes a duplicateMerge at most once per open period; the Propose ID derives from the Gap event (S:863).
      // T13.M2 · The proposal is made
      design: Propose  // S:811 "ContextMap Propose(duplicateMerge, source: this Gap, observed boundary versions from that event's finding)"
        triggered-by GapOpened  // S:811 "Boundary → ContextMap Propose(duplicateMerge" (policy BoundaryHandlingProposesDuplicateMerge)
      design: BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:851 "else → BoundaryChangeProposed"
      // T13.M3 · The architects are asked
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:882 "Recipient for a Gap source: all architects, cascading to admins and owners."
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:880 "BoundaryChangeProposed (not ratifiedInline, not withdrawn in the same write)" (policy BoundaryChangeProposedAsksQuestion)
      clarification: QuestionAsked  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule"
      // T13.M4 · An operator rejects
      clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Answer  // S:1124 "BoundaryChangeProposed → Ratify or Reject"
      clarification: QuestionResolved  // S:1034 "QuestionResolved {generation, resolution: an answer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy"
      design: Reject  // S:833 "Reject(proposal, answeredBy, answer ref)"
        triggered-by QuestionResolved  // S:1124 "BoundaryChangeProposed → Ratify or Reject" (policy RoutingProposalAnswerRejects)
      design: BoundaryChangeRejected  // S:859 "otherwise → BoundaryChangeRejected"
      design: DisposeGap  // S:822 "BoundaryChangeRejected → DisposeGap(Resolved{Distinct}), which is then Covered and not asked again (R2)"
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeRejected  // S:820 "Gap-sourced proposals (by ContextMap outcome)" (policy GapSourcedProposalRejectedDisposesGap)
      design: GapResolved  // S:752 "GapResolved {resolution, rationale?, computedBy?, carriedFrom?}"
      design: StartPass  // S:733 "StartPass(Convergence, scope: the customer workspace, model-wide)"
        triggered-by GapResolved  // S:729 "every Gap disposal (GapResolved, GapWaived or GapMooted)" (policy GapResolvedStartsConvergencePass)
      design: PassStarted [outcome]  // S:672 "PassStarted {startPosition, CorpusVersion, RulesVersion}"
      // T13.O13 · Settled (terminal)
      // note design: "The convergence read model folds the recorded events into the baseline and the inputs of the verdict"  // S:1002 "the convergence read model: the baseline per customer workspace"
      // PROVES: see the node before it; the verdict counts an open proposal or a blocking Gap (S:1002).
    when GapSourcedMergeWithdrawn
      // former flow: t13-a-gap-sourced-proposal-is-withdrawn.moment
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, its header: Separate flow of T13 (S:893 "A Gap source → the Gap disposal"). The increment that causes the withdrawal is any content write, rename or move of a construct in the read set (S:860, S:630); the cascade is the system's act, so it is not drawn as a command node. A later pass that still finds the duplicate reopens the Gap with fresh versions (S:823).
      // T13.M1 · A boundary Gap is found
      design: GapOpened  // S:811 "ContextMap Propose(duplicateMerge, source: this Gap"
      // A Boundary Gap proposes a duplicateMerge at most once per open period; the Propose ID derives from the Gap event (S:863).
      // T13.M2 · The proposal is made
      design: Propose  // S:811 "ContextMap Propose(duplicateMerge, source: this Gap, observed boundary versions from that event's finding)"
        triggered-by GapOpened  // S:811 "Boundary → ContextMap Propose(duplicateMerge" (policy BoundaryHandlingProposesDuplicateMerge)
      design: BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:851 "else → BoundaryChangeProposed"
      // T13.M3 · The architects are asked
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:882 "Recipient for a Gap source: all architects, cascading to admins and owners."
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:880 "BoundaryChangeProposed (not ratifiedInline, not withdrawn in the same write)" (policy BoundaryChangeProposedAsksQuestion)
      clarification: QuestionAsked  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule"
      // T13.M6 · Or the world changes under it
      design: ProposalWithdrawn  // S:845 "Every boundary version increment withdraws, **in the same write**, each open proposal whose read set contains an incremented construct"
      clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Withdrawn  // S:891 "ResolveQuestion(Withdrawn) for its ratification question, which closes it in flmnt"
        triggered-by ProposalWithdrawn  // S:891 "ResolveQuestion(Withdrawn) for its ratification question" (policy ProposalWithdrawnWithdrawsQuestion)
      clarification: QuestionResolved  // S:891 "ResolveQuestion(Withdrawn) for its ratification question, which closes it in flmnt"
      design: DisposeGap  // S:823 "ProposalWithdrawn → DisposeGap(Resolved{Fixed, rationale: SubjectChanged})"
        triggered-by ProposalWithdrawn  // S:820 "Gap-sourced proposals (by ContextMap outcome)" (policy GapSourcedProposalWithdrawnDisposesGap)
      design: GapResolved  // S:752 "GapResolved {resolution, rationale?, computedBy?, carriedFrom?}"
      design: StartPass  // S:733 "StartPass(Convergence, scope: the customer workspace, model-wide)"
        triggered-by GapResolved  // S:729 "every Gap disposal (GapResolved, GapWaived or GapMooted)" (policy GapResolvedStartsConvergencePass)
      design: PassStarted [outcome]  // S:672 "PassStarted {startPosition, CorpusVersion, RulesVersion}"
      // T13.O13 · Settled (terminal)
      // note design: "The convergence read model folds the recorded events into the baseline and the inputs of the verdict"  // S:1002 "the convergence read model: the baseline per customer workspace"
      // PROVES: see the node before it; the verdict counts an open proposal or a blocking Gap (S:1002).
    when NewRootAnswer
      // former flow: t13-a-new-root-answer-proposes-the-root-once.moment
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, its description: description "T13 — a NewRoot answer proposes the root once and accepts the first gathered Placement's provisional against it. Spec of record S:498-500, S:1116."
      // T13.M1·B1 · when the answer is a NewRoot
      clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Answer  // S:1028 "ResolveQuestion(answer + request Pointer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy)"
      clarification: QuestionResolved  // S:1116 the NewRoot answer to a missing-arm question
      design: ApplyAnswer  // S:498,1076 one ApplyAnswer(ImpliesBoundary{new}) on the first gathered Placement
        triggered-by QuestionResolved  // S:530 "An arm's context settled (Round 19" (policy ArmContextSettledAppliesAnswer)
      design: AnswerApplied  // S:437
      design: StoreConstruct  // S:498 policy 1: the root is stored (proposedFor: BoundaryRatification) and proposed once
        triggered-by AnswerApplied  // S:498 "1. StoreConstruct(proposedFor: BoundaryRatification) for each construct the change creates" (policy ImpliesBoundaryStoresCreatedConstructsOnAnswer)
      design: ConstructStored  // S:552
      design: ConstructLinked  // S:558 "StoreConstruct records it with ConstructStored (Placed; always"
      design: Propose  // S:499 policy 2: the Propose ID derives from this AnswerApplied
        triggered-by AnswerApplied  // S:499 "2. ContextMap Propose(change, source: the entry Pointer" (policy ImpliesBoundaryProposesOnAnswer)
      design: BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:851
      design: AcceptConstruct  // S:500 policy 3: AcceptConstruct(Answer{question}) on the first Placement's own provisional, whose arm is the proposed root
        triggered-by AnswerApplied  // S:500 "3. (a NewRoot answer only" (policy ImpliesBoundaryNewRootAcceptsProvisional)
      design: ConstructAccepted [outcome]  // S:553
      // Each other gathered Placement is applied as New with the proposed root as its arm and is committed when the root is (S:498); none is retired
      // while the root is proposed (S:498). The root's ratification continues as T13.M3 and T13.M4. NDD exit returns-to T13.M2.
      // T13.O13 · The boundary is settled (terminal)
      // note design: "The convergence read model folds the recorded events into the baseline and the inputs of the verdict"  // S:1002 the convergence read model: every ContextMap proposal that is open
      // PROVES: no open proposal in the convergence read model for the change (S:1002)
    when ProvisionalRetired
      // former flow: t13-a-provisional-boundary-construct-is-retired.moment
      // T13.M7 · A provisional boundary construct is retired
      design: AnswerApplied  // S:437,495-496 an answer that does not reuse a boundary-type provisional (the Return answer of a Defer{Divergence} included, S:860)
      design: RetireProvisional  // S:834,849 RetireProvisional(construct, cause Answered | Computed), system-only; increments that construct's boundary version, then cascades
      design: ProvisionalRetired  // S:841 {cause}
      design: SupersedeConstruct  // S:896 ProvisionalRetired -> SupersedeConstruct(by: none, cause: the cause it records)
        triggered-by ProvisionalRetired  // S:896 "ProvisionalRetired → SupersedeConstruct(by: none" (policy ProvisionalRetiredSupersedes)
      design: ConstructInvalidated [outcome]  // S:556
      // A repeat is a no-op (S:860). Also reached for the provisional of a Defer{Divergence} under SourceAuthority Conversation, with cause Computed
      // (S:860, T12).
      // T13.O13 · The boundary is settled (terminal)
      // note design: "The convergence read model folds the recorded events into the baseline and the inputs of the verdict"  // S:1002 the convergence read model: every ContextMap proposal that is open
      // PROVES: no open proposal in the convergence read model for the change (S:1002)
    when Retire
      // former flow: t13-a-retire-is-ratified.moment
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, its description: description "T13 — a retirement answer on a boundary construct is a Propose(retire), asked and ratified: the construct is superseded by none and creates nothing. Spec of record S:877, S:1111, S:862, S:883-885."
      // T13.M1 · A retirement is asked
      design: PlacementDecided  // S:512 "PlacementDecided, for a Placement whose entry's lineage names a superseded entry E → AskQuestion"
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:512 "AskQuestion (subject: the retirement subject for E"
        triggered-by PlacementDecided  // S:512 "Retirement (ruling 7090385c, Round 14):" (policy RetirementQuestionForSupersededEntry)
      clarification: QuestionAsked  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule"
      // T13.M2 · The retirement is answered
      clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Answer  // S:1111 "a PlacementDecided gathered by a retirement question"
      clarification: QuestionResolved  // S:1034 "QuestionResolved {generation, resolution: an answer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy"
      // T13.M3 · The proposal is made
      design: Propose  // S:1111 "ContextMap Propose(retire, or replace by X, source: the superseding entry's Pointer, created constructs: none"
        triggered-by PlacementDecided  // S:499 "2. ContextMap Propose(change, source: the entry Pointer" (policy ImpliesBoundaryProposes)
      design: BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:851 "else → BoundaryChangeProposed"
      // T13.M4 · An operator is asked
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:881 "otherwise all architects (cascading to admins and owners when there are none)"
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:880 "BoundaryChangeProposed (not ratifiedInline, not withdrawn in the same write)" (policy BoundaryChangeProposedAsksQuestion)
      clarification: QuestionAsked  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule"
      // T13.M5 · An operator ratifies
      clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Answer  // S:1124 "BoundaryChangeProposed → Ratify or Reject"
      clarification: QuestionResolved  // S:1034 "QuestionResolved {generation, resolution: an answer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy"
      design: Ratify  // S:832 "Ratify(proposal, answeredBy, answer ref)"
        triggered-by QuestionResolved  // S:1124 "BoundaryChangeProposed → Ratify or Reject" (policy RoutingProposalAnswerRatifies)
      design: BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:855 "otherwise → BoundaryChangeRatified"
      design: SupersedeConstruct  // S:885 "SupersedeConstruct(by: successor | none, cause: Ratified) for each construct the change retires"
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:885 "SupersedeConstruct(by: successor | none, cause: Ratified) for each construct the change retires" (policy BoundaryChangeRatifiedSupersedesRetired)
      design: ConstructInvalidated  // S:556 "ConstructInvalidated {cause, Pointer?, pass?}"
      design: StartPass  // S:733 "StartPass(Convergence, scope: the customer workspace, model-wide)"
        triggered-by ConstructInvalidated  // S:591 "ConstructSuperseded or ConstructInvalidated, as three policies on the one event" (policy ConstructInvalidatedStartsInvalidationPass)
      design: PassStarted [outcome]  // S:672 "PassStarted {startPosition, CorpusVersion, RulesVersion}"
      // T13.O13 · Settled (terminal)
      // note design: "The convergence read model folds the recorded events into the baseline and the inputs of the verdict"  // S:1002 "the convergence read model: the baseline per customer workspace"
      // PROVES: see the node before it; the verdict counts an open proposal or a blocking Gap (S:1002).

  moment "T13.M1 · A boundary change is stated or found (continued)" [branch]
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story
      design: StoreConstruct  // S:498 first policy: StoreConstruct(proposedFor: BoundaryRatification) for each construct the change creates
        triggered-by PlacementDecided  // S:498 "1. StoreConstruct(proposedFor: BoundaryRatification) for each construct the change creates" (policy ImpliesBoundaryStoresCreatedConstructs)
      design: ConstructStored  // S:552
      design: ConstructLinked  // S:558 "StoreConstruct records it with ConstructStored (Placed; always"
    when DuplicateMerge
      // former flow: t13-a-duplicate-merge-is-ratified.moment (path 1 of 2)
      // T13.M2 · The proposal is made
      design: Propose  // S:499,820 ContextMap Propose(change, source: the entry Pointer, created constructs, observed SubjectVersions)
        triggered-by PlacementDecided  // S:499 "2. ContextMap Propose(change, source: the entry Pointer" (policy ImpliesBoundaryProposes)
      design: BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:851 "else -> BoundaryChangeProposed" (versions current, no ratifiedBy)
      // T13.M3 · An operator is asked
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:880 BoundaryChangeProposed -> AskQuestion (subject: this event), only if the proposal is still open; recipient: the author if an operator, else all architects (S:881)
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:880 "BoundaryChangeProposed (not ratifiedInline, not withdrawn in the same write)" (policy BoundaryChangeProposedAsksQuestion)
      clarification: QuestionAsked  // S:1033 the question shows the boundary versions (S:880)
      // T13.M4 · An operator ratifies
      clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Answer  // S:1124 the answer to a BoundaryChangeProposed question routes to Ratify or Reject
      // T13.M4·B1 · when the answerer holds the operator role
      clarification: QuestionResolved  // S:1034
      // sees: no effect (Unauthorised) and a notice (S:1041-1042). NDD exit returns-to T13.M3: the question keeps its state (S:1042); the scenario ends at
      // the refusal here.
      // T13.M4·B2 · when the proposal is not open
      design: Ratify  // S:832,844
        triggered-by QuestionResolved  // S:1124 "BoundaryChangeProposed → Ratify or Reject" (policy RoutingProposalAnswerRatifies)
      design: BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:837,844
      design: SupersedeConstruct  // S:885,865 the newer duplicate is superseded by the older, the survivor (cause: Ratified)
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:885 "SupersedeConstruct(by: successor | none, cause: Ratified) for each construct the change retires" (policy BoundaryChangeRatifiedSupersedesRetired)
      design: ConstructSuperseded  // S:555
      design: MarkSameAs  // S:886 also MarkSameAs, carrying the proposal's addition when it has one
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:886 "for a duplicate merge, also MarkSameAs, carrying the proposal" (policy BoundaryChangeRatifiedMergesDuplicate)
      design: MarkedSameAs  // S:557
      design: AddAlias  // S:886,625 AddAlias on the survivor for each name of the newer duplicate
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:636 "BoundaryChangeRatified for a duplicateMerge → AddAlias on the survivor" (policy RatifiedDuplicateMergeAddsAliases)
      design: ConstructAliased [outcome]  // S:616
      // T13.O13 · The boundary is settled (terminal)
      // note design: "The convergence read model folds the recorded events into the baseline and the inputs of the verdict"  // S:1002 the convergence read model: every ContextMap proposal that is open
      // PROVES: no open proposal in the convergence read model for the change (S:1002)
    when DuplicateMergeWhenTheProposalIsNotOpen
