      // note design: "The convergence read model folds the recorded events into the baseline and the inputs of the verdict"  // S:1002 the convergence read model: every ContextMap proposal that is open
      // PROVES: no open proposal in the convergence read model for the change (S:1002)
    when Replace
      // former flow: t13-a-replacement-is-ratified.moment (path 1 of 2)
      // the first 4 node(s) are those of the main path
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, its header: Separate flow of T13 (T13.M4, change = replace). A retire (S:877) is the same without S-prime: SupersedeConstruct(by: none) and
      // carried from the former flow, its description: description "T13 — a replacement of a boundary construct is ratified: S-prime is accepted and S is superseded by it. Spec of record S:873, S:883-885."
      design: Ratify  // S:832,844 only an operator ratifies
        triggered-by QuestionResolved  // S:1124 "BoundaryChangeProposed → Ratify or Reject" (policy RoutingProposalAnswerRatifies)
      design: BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:837,844
      design: AcceptConstruct  // S:883 AcceptConstruct(Ratification) for each created construct
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:884 "AcceptConstruct(Ratification) for each created construct" (policy BoundaryChangeRatifiedAcceptsCreated)
      design: ConstructAccepted  // S:553
      // T13.M4·B2 · when the proposal is not open
      design: SupersedeConstruct  // S:885,862 S is retired by S-prime (cause: Ratified)
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:885 "SupersedeConstruct(by: successor | none, cause: Ratified) for each construct the change retires" (policy BoundaryChangeRatifiedSupersedesRetired)
      design: ConstructSuperseded [outcome]  // S:555
      // T13.O13 · The boundary is settled (terminal)
      // note design: "The convergence read model folds the recorded events into the baseline and the inputs of the verdict"  // S:1002 the convergence read model: every ContextMap proposal that is open
      // PROVES: no open proposal in the convergence read model for the change (S:1002)
    when ARatifyCascadeWithdrawsAProposalMadeStale
      // former flow: t13-a-ratification-cascade-withdraws-a-stale-proposal.moment
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, its description: description "T13 — The Ratify of one proposal increments boundary versions, and the cascade withdraws another open proposal whose observed versions are now stale, in the same write. Spec of record S:855, S:1333."
      // T13.M4·B3 · the proposal is open
      design: Ratify  // S:855 "otherwise → BoundaryChangeRatified. It increments"
      design: BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:855 "otherwise → BoundaryChangeRatified. It increments"
      design: ProposalWithdrawn [outcome]  // S:1335 "the write of Propose, Ratify, Reject or RetireProvisional (the cascade"
    when ARejectCascadeWithdrawsAProposalMadeStale
      // former flow: t13-a-rejection-cascade-withdraws-a-stale-proposal.moment
      // T13.M4·B3 · the proposal is open
      design: Reject  // S:859 "otherwise → BoundaryChangeRejected. It increments"
      design: BoundaryChangeRejected  // S:859 "otherwise → BoundaryChangeRejected. It increments"
      design: ProposalWithdrawn [outcome]  // S:1335 "the write of Propose, Ratify, Reject or RetireProvisional (the cascade"

  moment "T13.M4·B2 · when the proposal is not open (main path)"
    design: Ratify  // S:832,844 only an operator ratifies
      triggered-by QuestionResolved  // S:1124 "BoundaryChangeProposed → Ratify or Reject" (policy RoutingProposalAnswerRatifies)
    design: BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:837,844
    design: AcceptConstruct  // S:883 AcceptConstruct(Ratification) for each created construct
      triggered-by BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:884 "AcceptConstruct(Ratification) for each created construct" (policy BoundaryChangeRatifiedAcceptsCreated)
    design: ConstructAccepted  // S:553

  moment "T13.O13 · The boundary is settled (terminal)"
    note design: "The convergence read model folds the recorded events into the baseline and the inputs of the verdict"  // S:1002 the convergence read model: every ContextMap proposal that is open
    // PROVES: no open proposal in the convergence read model for the change (S:1002); the created constructs are accepted and committed or terminal;
    // boundary constructs are retired, replaced or renamed only through a ratified proposal (S:862)
